            <ArticleTitle>[A schedule for registration of pain in lumbago sciatica. A diagnostic aid].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3516-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is to be registered in the clinical setting. As a subjective phenomenon, pain can only be assessed, not measured exactly. In addition to being an important outcome variable, registration of pain can be used as an aid in diagnosis. A questionnaire has been worked out for evaluation of pain in lumbagosciatica, based upon findings from patients with radicular leg pain. The method is easy to use, and gives a three-dimensional picture of localization, quality, intensity and variability of the pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
